   "text": "Job one: get the work done. Why it matters: when people are not sure what is expected, work comes in late, gets redone, or quietly drops, and you find out on the due date. Four habits fix that. Plan it: before the quarter starts, pick three priorities, give each one an owner, and decide what moves if a new request lands. Say it: every person can tell you, without notes, what they own, by when, and what good looks like, and it is written where they can see it, not kept in your head. Check it: look at the work while it is in progress, in your weekly one-on-one, not the finished product on the due date. Fix it: when something breaks twice, find the cause and change something, instead of fixing it a third time yourself. What to stop doing: assuming the team knows, sending the goal in one email, checking only when it is late, and doing the work yourself because it is faster. This week: pick one person and confirm, out loud, what they own and by when. Now flip the four cards, then turn the page and make your first call."
