   "text": "Job three: make things better. Why it matters: Vanderbilt is asking every team to move faster and improve, and that does not happen from the top. It happens in your team, in small ways, every week. Four habits, and none of them is a reorganization. Explain the why: a new system is coming from central; tell your team the reason in your own words at Thursday’s meeting, before Tuesday’s campus email, and write down their objections to take back. Describe where you are going: in two sentences, what your team will be able to do next year that it cannot do now. Let people try: someone suggests a new way to run the weekly report; say, try it for two weeks and show me. Look back: ten minutes after any big piece of work, what worked, what did not, what changes, written where the next person can find it. What to stop doing: forwarding the announcement, and saying that is not how we do it here. This week: hold one ten-minute look-back. Now flip the cards, then turn the page; the new system is coming and the team already hates it."
